    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 204</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_204/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 05 Mar 2025 11:58:52 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_204/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Regarding the &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt; function, which of the following statements are correct:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A. A package can contain multiple &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt; functions;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B. When the program runs, &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt; functions of dependent packages are executed first, then &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt; functions within the &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; package;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C. The &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; package cannot have &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt; functions;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;D. An &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt; function can be called by other functions;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;A, B&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here are a few things to note about &lt;code&gt;init()&lt;/code&gt; functions:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 200</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_200/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 01 Mar 2025 02:08:44 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_200/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;When is the init() function executed?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Answer: &lt;code&gt;init()&lt;/code&gt; is executed before the &lt;code&gt;main()&lt;/code&gt; function.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Summary in one sentence: &lt;code&gt;import –&amp;gt; const –&amp;gt; var –&amp;gt; init() –&amp;gt; main()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If there are multiple init functions, the situation varies.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;execution-order-of-init-in-a-single-source-file&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Execution Order of init in a Single Source File&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#execution-order-of-init-in-a-single-source-file&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Conclusion: &lt;code&gt;The execution order of init functions within the same source file is consistent with their definition order, from top to bottom.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
